			"SHA": "f15b0b6c2e7c2b8e17d5ccb920680fc908052750"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-01-30T10:43:03Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				403,
				6
			],
			"Message": "feat(Wind/Integration): Replace Tauri fs plugin with Mountain backend file operations\n\nThis commit completes Wind's transition from direct filesystem API usage to full backend abstraction by replacing the Tauri fs plugin with Mountain's unified IPC interface for all file operations. This aligns with Land's architectural principle of delegating all privileged operations to the native Mountain backend through structured communication channels.\n\nKey changes include:\n- Refactored FileService to use `mountain_ipc_invoke` commands (`file:read`, `file:write`, `file:stat`, etc.) instead of direct Tauri fs plugin imports\n- Enhanced MountainIntegrationService with actual gRPC call implementation via `mountain_grpc_call` command, replacing simulation logic\n- Added comprehensive test suites for file operations and Mountain integration, ensuring robust error handling and type safety\n- Updated configuration sync to include client identification and sync metadata for better observability\n\nThese changes strengthen Wind's production readiness by establishing real communication with Mountain for filesystem operations, enabling centralized file management, enhanced security through backend delegation, and improved monitoring capabilities across the Land ecosystem.",
			"SHA": "c3042d3d1a625c53129373defd19a219f682418c"
		}
